<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly steady.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly steady.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mostly steady on Friday, traders said.</p>
<p>The two-month rate nudged down, while six months rose.</p>
<p>&quot;It's just an adjustment in prices,&quot; a foreign bank dealer said after foreign fund managers squared their positions on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;It was a quiet market,&quot; she said, since most funds are away for the Chinese New Year holidays.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  FEB 7		 FEB 6</p>
<p>    1 W		9 15/16		 9 15/16</p>
<p>    2 W		9 15/16		 9 15/16</p>
<p>    1 M		10  1/8		 10  1/8</p>
<p>    2 M		10  1/8		 10  3/16</p>
<p>    3 M		10  3/16		10  3/16</p>
<p>    6 M		10  1/4		 10  3/16</p>
<p>    12M		10  7/16		10  7/16</p>
<p>    VAL		10-Feb		  7-Feb</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937</p>
</text>
